@cc [owner:spolu,label:backend;error-handling] preserve-fdb-retry-errors
Within retrying transactions, FDB transaction failures MUST reach `Database::run` unchanged through
every resource and API conversion so the runner can decide whether to retry. They MUST NOT be
swallowed, stringified, or converted to domain errors or API statuses before the runner returns.

@cc [owner:spolu,label:backend;error-handling] transaction-domain-errors
A transaction closure returning a resource or stored-data decoding failure MUST abort its attempt
without committing or retrying.
`fdb::with_transaction` MUST preserve the typed error returned by its closure through the runner.
API closures MAY translate non-FDB failures to their API status before returning them.
